//  M.A.U.S. UTILITY UNIT -- PLACEHOLDER BODY VARIANT
//
//  Without a monsterpart matching this monstertype's category and part slot,
//  <partImage> in the animation resolves to nothing and the unit spawns with no
//  art. This file is what makes the drone visible.
//
//  WHERE THIS FILE LIVES
//
//  Monsterparts sit in a subfolder of the monstertype's directory named after
//  the part TYPE. With the monstertype at /monsters/nicemice_ship_pets/ and a
//  part slot called "body", this belongs in:
//
//    /monsters/nicemice_ship_pets/body/
//
//  Monsters with several slots get one folder each -- penguin soldiers keep
//  arms, bodies, hats and weapons in parallel directories. The png named in
//  "frames" resolves relative to THIS file, so it lives in the same folder.
//
//  HOW THE BINDING WORKS
//
//    "category" -> must match an entry in the monstertype's "categories"
//    "type"     -> must match an entry in the monstertype's "parts"
//    "frames"   -> maps animation part NAME to a png in this directory
//
//  The engine collects every monsterpart matching category + type and picks one
//  at random when the unit is instantiated, which is how petbunny gets its black
//  / blackwhite variants. Adding more chassis later means dropping more
//  .monsterpart files in beside this one -- no changes to the monstertype.
//
//  NAME THE PNGS AFTER THE VARIANT, NOT THE SLOT. Every unit type sharing this
//  parent directory shares this body/ folder, separated only by "category". A
//  generic body.png would be claimed by whichever type got there first, so
//  petbunny's convention -- black.png, blackwhite.png -- is load-bearing rather
//  than stylistic.
//
//  Both keys in "frames" correspond to parts declared in the animation:
//  "body" is the world-lit base layer, "bodyfullbright" the glow layer drawn
//  over it. Point both at the same placeholder png for now; split them when
//  real art exists.
//
//  NOTE ON VARIANT PERSISTENCE: which monsterpart gets chosen follows from the
//  monster's seed. groundPet.lua hands that seed to its anchor via setPet, but
//  the station currently discards it -- so a unit may change appearance when it
//  respawns. Worth resolving before more than one variant exists.

{
  "name" : "drone_placeholder",
  "category" : "nicemice_ship_pet_drone",
  "type" : "body",

  "frames" : {
    "body" : "body_0_lit.png",
    "bodyfullbright" : "body_0_fullbright.png"
  }
}
